+# ExecPlan 089 — P10-03 local packaged-release readiness
+
+## Goal and user-visible outcome
+
+Run one local HTTP smoke against the installed release wheel and normal built
+web/PWA assets, then reconcile the existing Phase 10 acceptance requirements.
+Phase 10 remains in progress pending review.
+
+## Why now
+
+P10-01 corrected frontend artifact verification and P10-02 proved a bounded
+TEST backup/restore. Neither exercised the packaged API and built frontend
+together through actual HTTP.
+
+## In scope
+
+- One normal `pnpm build` using the locked offline API package check.
+- One owned, loopback TEST API and disposable current-migration database.
+- Public assets, authentication, readiness, Settings read/write, logout,
+  unknown API errors, static-root privacy and safe operational logs.
+- A compact requirement-to-evidence reconciliation and local run instructions.
+
+## Explicit non-goals
+
+No Android rebuild/device run, provider call, catalog import, development or
+production database operation, home access, dependency download, deployment,
+application commit or main push. This is not a full security audit or production
+disaster-recovery test.
+
+## Current repository state
+
+Start from `main` at `6b844b757ec2df2dd3ebcdbc32f2e6ccbf7ddb19` with an
+empty index. The three pre-existing protected dirty files remain untouched.
+P10-01 and P10-02 are accepted and closed; Phase 10 remains in progress.
+
+## Decisions and assumptions
+
+Use the existing `pnpm build` path, its isolated `.local/package-check` venv,
+and the existing owned TEST database helpers. Select the exact new package-check
+receipt from this build. A child started with that venv's `python -I` binds an
+OS-assigned loopback port and reports its installed-package import path. The
+runner owns the child handle and exact disposable database, and leaves private
+evidence only under ignored `.local` paths.
+
+## Data model and API/interface changes
+
+No product schema or API change. Add a root-only `test:packaged-release` task
+that takes the selected package-check `result.json` path; it is a release check,
+not a development-serving path.
+
+## Implementation sequence
+
+1. Add the guarded packaged HTTP runner and focused refusal tests.
+2. Add its task entrypoint and concise local instructions.
+3. Run one current build, select its new package receipt, and run one smoke.
+4. Record results, limits and the existing Phase 10 evidence table; publish the
+   review package without committing implementation files.
+
+## Validation and acceptance criteria
+
+The installed `brickvault_api` import must resolve inside the isolated venv,
+never `services/api/src`. HTTP must serve the actual built shell/assets,
+deny protected reads before and after the authenticated session, permit one
+CSRF-protected Settings update and readback, keep unknown `/api` errors JSON,
+keep private responses uncached, reject static-root probes, and log operational
+metadata without secret values. Run focused new-tooling tests, targeted static
+checks and `git diff --check`; reuse unchanged accepted evidence.
+
+## Security, privacy and data integrity
+
+Generate the TEST password only in memory. Pass the database target to the
+child through a restricted environment, never command arguments or reports.
+Keep raw logs and ledgers ignored. Preserve all three protected dirty files
+byte-for-byte and unstaged. Never publish a dump, credential, cookie, token,
+private record or raw private log.
+
+## Failure modes, rollback and recovery
+
+Refuse package receipts outside the exact ignored package-check tree, unverified
+receipts or source-checkout imports. On failure, stop the exact child, remove
+only the run-recorded ownership-marked database, return the existing TEST
+container to its initial state and retain a private cleanup ledger. If cleanup
+cannot be proved, report the exact ledger and stop rather than deleting by
+prefix or touching another service.
+
+## Progress log
+
+- [x] 2026-09-28: Scope and initial state inspected; implementation authorized.
+- [x] 2026-09-28: One current build and packaged HTTP smoke completed.
+- [x] 2026-09-28: Five focused refusal tests and targeted Python/JavaScript
