+| Backup and restore | P10-02's accepted real PostgreSQL custom dump/restore passed one focused TEST integration proof, eight guard tests and exact cleanup. | No repeat; the packaged smoke uses a fresh disposable database. | None for the requested disposable proof. Production retention, off-host backup, role/configuration backup and disaster recovery remain outside this local gate. |
+| Observability and release operation | Accepted foundation HTTP/request-ID, Host/Origin, JSON error, safe-log and owned-resource cleanup evidence. | Nineteen structured request events included useful route/status results without TEST secrets; unknown `/api` returned JSON, and the exact API child/database were removed with the TEST container restored. The local command and limits are documented in `LOCAL_DEVELOPMENT.md`. | None for local operation. Centralized monitoring, deployment and production rollback belong to later approval. |
+
+## Actual P10-03 run and limits
+
+On Windows with Node 24.14.0, pnpm 11.8.0 and Python 3.13.12, the single
+`pnpm build` succeeded. The new isolated package-check receipt selected the
+installed wheel, and one successful `pnpm test:packaged-release` smoke passed
+18 HTTP checks, including two referenced built assets and three static-root
+probes. The child import was verified under the selected venv's
+`Lib/site-packages/brickvault_api/__init__.py`, not `services/api/src`. Its
+ignored ledger reports 19 safe request events, one exact database removed,
+API stopped, prior TEST service state restored and zero leftovers. The TEST
+password existed only in memory. No provider, development/production database,
+home server, Android build/device, deployment or main push was used.
+
+The first smoke invocation refused Windows separators in the package receipt
+before creating a database. The next invocation rejected a relative receipt
+at the existing private-path guard, also before provisioning. A later
+invocation exposed the Windows venv launcher/worker PID distinction; its owned
+TEST database was removed and the service state restored. The runner now
+retains an OS handle to the exact installed worker and confirms listener
+closure. The final successful smoke
+used the unchanged successful build; no second build or historical test
+campaign was run.
+
+**Verdict: READY FOR PHASE 10 CLOSEOUT REVIEW.** This is a request to review
+the existing local Phase 10 evidence, not a claim that Phase 10 is closed or
